+/*
+ * Resume lab knobs (single experimental vehicle, kernel/power/main.c).
+ * Sysfs writes under /sys/power/ take effect on the NEXT suspend; the
+ * in-progress resume always finishes with whatever mode it started with
+ * (each mode reads pm_bringup_mode once, right after wake, and again at
+ * suspend_finish() -- do not rely on the two reads staying consistent if
+ * you rewrite this mid-cycle from a script; change it, then trigger one
+ * suspend, don't race the two).
+ *
+ * pm_bringup_mode:
+ *   0 = stock thaw_secondary_cpus() at Enable_cpus. Control/baseline,
+ *       byte-for-byte the original behavior.
+ *   1 = kick nothing at Enable_cpus; a background kthread brings every
+ *       frozen CPU fully online, one at a time, strictly sequentially,
+ *       after user space is thawed and the console is back. SMT-order
+ *       safe by construction (sequential, one CPU at a time), but trades
+ *       that for a different, real hazard: every ONLINE transition now
+ *       races live userspace and a fully-resumed device tree -- the
+ *       shape of the 2014 Lan Tianyu RFC that Zijlstra/Wysocki rejected
+ *       upstream. Kept to measure that hazard fairly on this hardware,
+ *       not as a shipping candidate.
+ *   2 = kick every frozen CPU concurrently at Enable_cpus (including SMT
+ *       siblings of the same physical core), finalize to ONLINE
+ *       synchronously in suspend_finish(), under the freezer. NOT
+ *       SMT-safe: see the comment on pm_bringup_kick() in kernel/cpu.c.
+ *       Kept only as a fast/best-case reference point, not a shipping
+ *       candidate -- do not run this unattended.
+ *   3 = like 2, but stages the kick: only primary threads are kicked at
+ *       Enable_cpus; their siblings are kicked later, in
+ *       pm_finalize_cpu_resume(), strictly after every primary has
+ *       reached CPUHP_ONLINE. SMT-safe. On a frozen set that is a single
+ *       primary and its own sibling (this machine, always), expect a
+ *       modest win bounded by the device-resume window, not mode 2's
+ *       numbers -- the sibling's cost is never overlapped with anything
+ *       here, same as stock.
+ *
+ * pm_affskip: skip redundant kthread re-affining during the ONLINE walk
+ *   (default on). Independent of pm_bringup_mode; applies to any CPU
+ *   hotplug online event, not just resume.
+ * pm_cpufreq_defer: defer cpufreq_resume() past the ONLINE walk whenever
+ *   a non-stock mode leaves CPUs not yet online at the point stock would
+ *   have already finished (see pm_resume_cpu_online_pending() in
+ *   kernel/cpu.c). Inert under mode 0.
