+ * (primaries only). Pass 2 then kicks and finishes the sibling threads --
+ * only once every primary in the frozen set has reached CPUHP_ONLINE, so
+ * only once it is certain no primary is still inside its microcode-
+ * sensitive window. Expect this mode's overlap benefit to be bounded by
+ * how much of the primary's own bring-up latency fits behind the device-
+ * resume window that ran between the kick and this call: on a frozen set
+ * that is a single primary plus its own sibling (this machine, always),
+ * the sibling's cost is never overlapped with anything and stays fully
+ * serial, same as stock -- do not expect this mode to reproduce mode 2's
+ * headline numbers, if any; it is only claiming the smaller, real,
+ * SMT-safe part of that win.
